# Review: TablePlugin

The editing surface is solid: `TableArticle` wires inline editing, row insertion, multi-select
delete, column delete, save, export, sort and tag filters from the view's query AST, and global
search filtering; `TableCard` renders a read-only, selection-free grid. `create`, `addRow` and
`handleTypeAdded` are implemented. The `onCreateSpace` hook does not exist at all, so no default
Task table is made. The Table skill has a one-line instruction and no tools, so an agent cannot
create tables through it. The plugin's own test only checks module activation; the behaviour tests
that exist live in `react-ui-table` (selection, sort persistence) and `@dxos/schema` (view from
typename).

Of 35 items: 7 done, 16 untested, 5 partial, 3 diverged, 4 missing. Findings:

- **onCreateSpace / F-1.3 / T-5 are missing.** plugin-table contributes no OnCreateSpace capability;
  only the TableCard story seeds a table in its own `onCreateSpace` callback.
- **F-6.2 diverged.** `TableSkill` declares `tools: []`, so the agent has no table tool;
  the source says table ops are handled by generic schema ops.
- **Header sort is persisted to local view state, not the View query AST** (T-3), per
  `table-model.test.ts`; the query-AST sort is only read, never written by a header click.

